docs {
  Drive the wiggly-gin API by hand, one click at a time.
  
  Start the server, then select the `local` environment. Open Seats and send Create
  game, then Join game. Those two requests record the game id and both seat tokens as
  runtime variables, so no later request needs anything typed into it.
  
  A runtime variable lives in Bruno for this session only. It is never written to disk,
  so playing a game leaves the files in this folder unchanged, and no seat token is ever
  committed.
  
  Host and Guest hold the same seven requests, one folder for each seat. Send Look in
  either folder to read that player's own view of the game. The view names the phase, so
  it tells you which move that player can make next.
  
  Discard and Knock each need a card you hold. Read your hand in Look, then set the
  `rank` and `suit` variables in the `local` environment. Both moves read them.
  
  Refusals holds one request for each way the server says no.
  
  The shapes are described in `docs/openapi.yaml`, which is the authority on all of them.
}
